  ],
  "notes": "RE-AUTHORED. Still a LOOP, not a sequence: each cycle is clay -> monument -> Abelard, and the quest only completes after all seventeen. 0x056 gives no per-tablet progress, so no ladder can count them. But the claim that 'the wiki does not list where' was WRONG -- it lists every one, with zone and grid, under a sibling '====The Monuments====' heading the prepass used to cut away. So step 2's single zone-less Stone Monument (a nil-zone row, the kind that matches everywhere) becomes seventeen properly zoned ones sharing a group, all drawn at once, which is right because you may do them in any order.\n\nThe Clay Tablet evidence sits on the LAST group member rather than on all seventeen: duplicate evidence across steps is a hard gate, and it has to be the last one so that satisfying it lands the mark on Abelard rather than back inside the group. Holding clay draws the monuments; holding a tablet draws Abelard, which is exactly the loop.\n\nThe three Shadowreign monuments under 'The Monuments in the Past' are deliberately NOT steps -- the page says trading them gets no response from Abelard.",
